  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — identifying probable outcomes based on probability > 1/n and computing the average of such outcomes — is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not mention the threshold (1/n), nor does the individual categorize outcomes as probable or not. Instead, the individual computes expected value and, when equal, prefers a smaller loss. This reflects a different decision rationale (expected value with loss aversion), not the specified reason involving probable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The justification does not align with the rule of the reason (which compares the average of probable outcomes), even though both lotteries have one probable outcome (0 Euros) and thus equal average probable outcomes. The absence of any reference to the threshold or the classification of outcomes as probable means the reason was not applied. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
